    {# And today #}
    <section class="section">
      <div class="conteneur"><div class="mesure-lecture">
        <h2>And today?</h2>
        <p>
          A hundred and thirty years after it appeared, the traditional AZERTY still writes French without an accented capital in a single keystroke, without œ and without French quotation marks. Two paths of correction now exist: the 2019 AFNOR standard, an ambitious overhaul whose adoption remains marginal, and the corrective layouts that keep the letters A to Z in place and fix only what is missing. <strong>AZERTY Global</strong> belongs to the second: five changes, a smooth transition, and every character this page has just described finally within reach.
        </p>
